From 03917ef1833b8f8c814ab37431b0749ff2c2dbad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:42:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gallium/pvr: varyings on the native draw path

- Allocate fragment shader inputs as the Vulkan driver does: z/w first,
  then each varying slot in location order, four coefficient registers
  per component.
- Build the coefficient program (one DOUTI iterator per z, w and varying,
  reading the vertex shader's vtxout offset) per fragment variant and
  vertex shader, and point TA VARYINGBASE at it. Flat varyings follow the
  rasterizer's provoking vertex.
- TA VARYING0 takes the vertex shader's f32 smooth/flat/npc counts, and
  output select takes the fragment shader's z/w use.
- PDS SIZEINFO takes dword counts, as the reference divides them; the
  byte counts made the PDS and USC varying sizes four times too large.
- Advertise 16 varyings and the vertex/fragment output limits; with none,
  every program with a varying failed to link.

gltri GLTRI_VARYING=1 (v = pos * 0.5 + 0.5 into gl_FragColor) gives the
exact expected colour at four sample points, as zink does.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_csb.c    |   9 +-
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_csb.h    |  21 ++--
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_draw.c   | 110 +++++++++++++++++++-
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c  |   2 +-
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c |   7 ++
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_shader.c |  47 +++++++++
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_shader.h |  17 +++
 7 files changed, 192 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

